<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <!--
    The shared syntax library of the shared JavaScript libraries programme (milestone SJL-13.2; Broiler.VM's
    JSD-0083, decisions D6 to D17 and D32, under the contract of JSD-0080): the frontend's syntax half - the request,
    the tokenizer, the tree, the parser and the diagnostics in Broiler.ECMAScript.Syntax, and from stage 4d the
    declarations walk in Broiler.ECMAScript.Semantics - built in six stages, a to f, one merge each. It names neither
    engine and reads no culture.

    Stage SJL-13.2a's skeleton holds the contract's types: the parse request (source, goal, switches, the inherited
    context of eval code, proposal flags, the lexer extension, limits and providers) and the diagnostics' types.
    Stage SJL-13.2b adds the tokenizer, internal to the library: the lexical grammar of ECMA-262 clause 12 under the
    goal its caller names, and a parse entry that refuses a source the lexical grammar refuses and answers "not
    implemented" for every other. Stage SJL-13.2c adds the tree, public and immutable, and the parser, internal: the
    syntactic grammar of every goal, with cover grammars converted and the two limits checked before the stack is;
    the parse entry answers accepted, with the tree, or refused. Stage SJL-13.2d gives every refusal its catalogue
    row's code and adds the declarations walk in Broiler.ECMAScript.Semantics, the parse-time early errors and the side
    tables; stage SJL-13.2e derives the limits and adds determinism and fuzzing; stage SJL-13.2f, the done-when, charges
    every chain node its whole height in tree depth (the owner's decision of 2026-11-02 on decision D14) and packs the
    library.

    References (decision D6; rule SL1's row Frontend -> [Algorithms, Broiler.Unicode.Algorithms]):
    Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms, whose WorkCharge and DepthLimit the request takes and whose
    NumericLiterals.Evaluate the tokenizer calls (decision D9: no change to that library at SJL-13), and
    Broiler.Unicode.Algorithms, whose IUnicodeTables is the request's Unicode provider (decision D8). No
    Broiler.Regex: the regular-expression validator is an interface of this library that each engine supplies
    (decision D7). No engine, and nothing of Broiler.VM.

    PACKED FROM STAGE SJL-13.2f, the done-when (decision D6): IsPackable was false from stage 4a to 4e, so that no
    version of the shared stream carries part of the library, and is true now, on the shared stream's 0.1.0-preview.N
    scheme with the other shared packages, with package validation as they have it (a first version, validated without
    a baseline). Publishing that version is the owner's, with the owner's approval (decision D30).
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Broiler.ECMAScript.Syntax</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Broiler.ECMAScript.Frontend</AssemblyName>
    <PackageId>Broiler.ECMAScript.Frontend</PackageId>
    <Description>The shared syntax library of the Broiler JavaScript engines (ECMA-262): an immutable parse request with goals, switches, the inherited context of eval code, proposal flags, a lexer extension, limits and providers (Broiler.Unicode's tables, a regular-expression validator each engine supplies, an optional work meter), an immutable syntax tree with full spans and raw facts, and diagnostics with shared codes, message identifiers, phases and spans. The tokenizer reads the lexical grammar of ECMA-262 and the parser its syntactic grammar for scripts, modules, eval code and the dynamic function's parameters and body, with cover grammars converted, the declarations walk reports the parse-time early errors with side tables of each scope's declarations, and the nesting depth and tree depth are checked before the stack is.</Description>
    <PackageTags>broiler;ecmascript;javascript;shared;frontend;parser;syntax;ecma-262</PackageTags>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms\Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms.csproj" />
    <PackageReference Include="Broiler.Unicode.Algorithms" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Broiler.ECMAScript.Frontend.Tests" />
    <!-- The Native AOT probe reads the tree's children and the token stream for the canonical dump that compares the JIT
         and Native AOT parses (stage SJL-13.2e, runners/SyntaxDump.cs); it calls nothing else internal. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Broiler.ECMAScript.Probe" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
